  "cves": [
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-97209",
      "publishedDate": "2026-10-30T08:59:17.615Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-10-30T09:01:05.212Z",
      "description": "Insecure Temporary File vulnerability in Mix deps.partition in Elixir allows a local user to execute code as another user via a swapped partition config file. Partitioned dependency compilation passes the project configuration to each partition VM through a file in a fixed-name directory under the shared system temporary directory, and the partition trusts what it reads back. Another local user on the same host can exploit this during a mix deps.compile run that uses partitioned compilation.\n\nMix.Tasks.Deps.Partition.server/4 in lib/mix/lib/mix/tasks/deps.partition.ex creates the directory with File.mkdir_p/1, which accepts an existing directory without checking its owner, so a user who created it first can replace the file before client/0 reads it.\n\nThis issue affects mix: from 1.20.0-rc.4 before 1.20.5.",
      "severity": "N/A",
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：elixir-lang elixir\n🔓 漏洞类型：CWE-377 (CWE-377)\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
